    "name": "cubic BSiN3-derived tetrahedral nitride (ordered B/Si on cation sublattice)",
    "hypothesis": "A fully tetrahedral, wide-gap nitride near BSiN3 composition could exist as an ordered derivative of diamond-like AB networks, using alternating short B-N and longer Si-N bonds to preserve local valence balance while increasing bond ionicity relative to SiC. This is a crystal-structure hypothesis only; no direct synthesis or prior isolation evidence was provided in the supplied sources, so stability and order are uncertain.",
