    "expected_advantage": "If realizable as a dense ordered nitride, the all-light-element tetrahedral bonding could be favorable for dielectric behavior and heat transport, while avoiding oxygen-rich glassy chemistry that often lowers thermal transport in thin films.",
    "closest_known_material": "BN zincblende and AlN zincblende, as tetrahedral wide-gap nitride reference points; also SiN_x thin films as a practical process reference.",
    "falsification_test": "Attempt deposition in the B-Si-N composition space by reactive sputtering or PECVD followed by annealing. If XRD/TEM fail to show a reproducible crystalline ordered phase and spectroscopy instead indicates only amorphous SiN_x with B incorporation or phase-separated BN/Si3N4-like regions, this hypothesis is falsified as a distinct crystal candidate under those conditions.",
